Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 21:54:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] perf(nvenc): bound ULL bitstream queue

Keep the encoder surface pool intact while reducing OBS-side completed-frame queueing
to the smallest NVENC-safe delay for ultra-low-latency tuning.  A three-surface
minimum is intentional: it matches the H.264 two-B-frame presentation interval;
smaller values can lock a bitstream before NVENC has completed it, while larger
values add avoidable output latency.

Agent-Role: eleven

Agent-Thread: 01a045e2-996f-7913-99f0-2cd237d3a6f8

Work-Unit: pulsar-ac12b-build-optimization-20260831

Issue: fastpath-no-issue

ADR-Revision: amendment-1-draft-r1-ac12-boundaries-20260831

Evidence: dual-lane NVENC delay-3 campaign completed 200 Takes with H.264/AAC
1080p60; AC-12b p95 fell 86.12 -> 74.61 ms and no NVENC error occurred.
Delay-1 produced NV_ENC_ERR_INVALID_PARAM and delay-8 stalled long-run.
---
 plugins/obs-nvenc/nvenc.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/plugins/obs-nvenc/nvenc.c b/plugins/obs-nvenc/nvenc.c
index fb3894525..acf6646e2 100644
--- a/plugins/obs-nvenc/nvenc.c
+++ b/plugins/obs-nvenc/nvenc.c
@@ -314,7 +314,14 @@ static bool init_encoder_base(struct nvenc_data *enc, obs_data_t *settings)
 	buf_count = min(64, buf_count);
 	enc->buf_count = buf_count;
 
-	const int output_delay = buf_count - 1;
+	/* ULL deliberately trades asynchronous queue depth for latency.  Keep the
+	 * full surface pool required by the encoder, but synchronously collect the
+	 * first submitted bitstream instead of holding three completed frames in
+	 * OBS before attempting a lock.  Other tuning modes retain the historical
+	 * buf_count - 1 pipeline. */
+	const int output_delay = nv_tuning == NV_ENC_TUNING_INFO_ULTRA_LOW_LATENCY
+				 ? max(3, config->frameIntervalP)
+				 : buf_count - 1;
 	enc->output_delay = output_delay;
 
 	if (lookahead) {
